-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, "Effect of guaranteed minimum pension
-- on social security benefits" and "Final provisions" (sections 18 to 21).
--
-- Section 22 (short title, commencement and extent) is in spc-dates.l4, where the
-- dates of the Act are kept. Section 18A is the one provision here that matters to
-- a claimant: it lets a pilot scheme switch off or change any provision of the Act.

§ `Effect of guaranteed minimum pension on social security benefits`

§§ `18 Equal treatment for widows and widowers`

-- Section 18 amends section 47(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 so that the
-- widower of an earner is treated like a widow in the reference to a person
-- entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension. It changes another Act, not this
-- Act's rules on state pension credit, and it asks no question of a claimant.
-- src:320 | In section 47(1) of the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (c. 48) (which limits the width of the reference in section 46(1) to a person entitled to a guaranteed minimum pension by virtue of being the widower of an earner)—
-- src:321 | (a) after “an earner” insert “ in any case where he is entitled to a benefit other than a widowed parent’s allowance ”;
-- src:322 | (b) for paragraph (a) substitute—
-- src:323 | (a) he is also entitled to a Category B retirement pension by virtue of the earner’s contributions (or would be so entitled but for section 43(1) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992); or
-- src:324 | and
-- src:325 | (c) in paragraph (b), for “section 41(7)” substitute “ section 41(5) ” and for “the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992” substitute “ that Act ”.
-- (not encoded: section 18 amends the Pension Schemes Act 1993)

§ `Final provisions`

§§ `18A Pilot schemes`

-- Section 18A(1): regulations to which the section applies may be made to have
-- effect for a specified period "not exceeding 12 months". A period of 12 months
-- starting on a day ends on the day before that day a year later, so a scheme
-- that starts on a day may end on any day BEFORE the same calendar day in the next
-- year (the fork is registered in NOTES.md, F-14). The lenient `Date` constructor
-- carries a start on 29 February to 1 March of the next year.
-- src:328 | (1) Any regulations to which this subsection applies may be made so as to have effect for a specified period not exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 18A(1) (src:328)
GIVEN `the first day of the pilot scheme` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the pilot scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18A(1) -- the period of the pilot scheme does not exceed 12 months` `the first day of the pilot scheme` `the last day of the pilot scheme` MEANS
        `the last day of the pilot scheme` AT LEAST `the first day of the pilot scheme`
    AND `the last day of the pilot scheme` LESS THAN
            Date (DATE_DAY `the first day of the pilot scheme`)
                 (DATE_MONTH `the first day of the pilot scheme`)
                 (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the pilot scheme` PLUS 1)

-- Section 18A(2) to (4): the section reaches only regulations made under this Act
-- or under section 1 or 5 of the Administration Act, and only if made with a view
-- to finding out whether their provisions will make it more likely that persons
-- entitled to claim state pension credit will claim it, or receive it. A judgment
-- about why regulations were made, handed to the Secretary of State; a claimant
-- is not asked it.
--
-- Section 18A(5), (6): a pilot scheme may provide that any provision of this Act
-- (or section 1 of the Administration Act) does not apply, or applies with
-- modifications, and may make different provision for different cases. The
-- consequence for a claimant: if a pilot scheme applies to the claimant's case the
-- Act's own rules for entitlement and amount may not decide it. Whether one applies
-- is a fact the claimant states, because it depends on the scheme's area, class of
-- person and selection (subsection (8)), none of which is among the inputs.
-- src:329 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), subsection (1) applies to—
-- src:330 | (a) regulations made under this Act, and
-- src:331 | (b) regulations made under section 1 or 5 of the Administration Act.
-- src:332 | (3) Subsection (1) only applies to regulations if they are made with a view to ascertaining whether their provisions will—
-- src:333 | (a) make it more likely that persons who are entitled to claim state pension credit will do so;
-- src:334 | (b) make it more likely that persons who are entitled to claim state pension credit will receive it.
-- src:335 | (4) Regulations which, by virtue of subsection (1), are to have effect for a limited period are referred to in this section as a “pilot scheme”.
-- src:336 | (5) A pilot scheme may, in particular—
-- src:337 | (a) provide for a relevant provision not to apply, or to apply with modifications, for the purposes of the pilot scheme, and
-- src:338 | (b) make different provision for different cases or circumstances.
-- src:339 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (5)(a), a “relevant provision” is—
-- src:340 | (a) any provision of this Act, and
-- src:341 | (b) section 1 of the Administration Act.
@ref s 18A(2) to (6) (src:329-341)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18A(5) -- a pilot scheme may displace provisions of the Act for the case` case MEANS
    case's `a pilot scheme under section 18A applies`

-- Section 18A(7) to (11): what a pilot scheme may provide about disregarding
-- payments made under it, areas, classes of person, sampling, cessation, renewal,
-- and Treasury consent. Powers; no pilot scheme is among the inputs.
-- src:342 | (7) A pilot scheme may provide that no account is to be taken of any payment made under the pilot scheme in considering a person's—
-- src:343 | (a) liability to tax,
-- src:344 | (b) entitlement to benefit under an enactment relating to social security (irrespective of the name or nature of the benefit), or
-- src:345 | (c) entitlement to a tax credit.
-- src:346 | (8) A pilot scheme may provide that its provisions are to apply only in relation to—
-- src:347 | (a) one or more specified areas or localities;
-- src:348 | (b) one or more specified classes of person;
-- src:349 | (c) persons selected—
-- src:350 | (i) by reference to prescribed criteria, or
-- src:351 | (ii) on a sampling basis.
-- src:352 | (9) A pilot scheme may make consequential or transitional provision with respect to the cessation of the scheme on the expiry of the specified period.
-- src:353 | (10) A pilot scheme may be replaced by a further pilot scheme making the same or similar provision.
-- src:354 | (11) The power of the Secretary of State to make regulations which, by virtue of this section, are to have effect for a limited period is exercisable only with the consent of the Treasury.
-- (not encoded: section 18A(7) to (11) are powers and a consent requirement)

§§ `19 Regulations and orders`

-- Section 19 applies the parliamentary procedure of section 175 of the
-- Contributions and Benefits Act to this Act's regulation-making powers, says
-- which first regulations need an affirmative resolution, and makes the rest
-- subject to annulment. It governs the Secretary of State and Parliament, and
-- asks nothing of a claimant. It came into force on the passing of the Act
-- (section 22(2)).
-- src:356 | (1) Subject to the following provisions of this section, subsections (1), (2) to (5) and (10) of section 175 of the Contributions and Benefits Act (regulations and orders etc) shall apply in relation to any power conferred on the Secretary of State by any provision of this Act to make regulations or an order as they apply in relation to any power conferred on him by that Act to make regulations or an order, but as if for references to that Act (other than references to specific provisions of it) there were substituted references to this Act.
-- src:357 | (2) A statutory instrument containing (whether alone or with other provisions) the first regulations under—
-- src:358 | (a) section 2(3)(b), (4) or (6),
-- src:359 | (b) section 3(4), (5), (6), (7) or (8),
-- src:360 | (c) section 4(3),
-- src:361 | (d) section 12, or
-- src:362 | (e) section 15(1)(e), (f) or (j), (2), (3), (4) or (6),
-- src:363 | shall not be made unless a draft of the instrument has been laid before, and approved by a resolution of, each House of Parliament.
-- src:364 | (2A) A statutory instrument containing regulations which, by virtue of section 18A, are to have effect for a limited period shall not be made unless a draft of the instrument has been laid before, and approved by a resolution of, each House of Parliament.
-- src:365 | (3) A statutory instrument—
-- src:366 | (a) which contains regulations under this Act (whether alone or with other provisions), and
-- src:367 | (b) which is not subject to any requirement that a draft of the instrument be laid before, and approved by a resolution of, each House of Parliament,
-- src:368 | shall be subject to annulment in pursuance of a resolution of either House of Parliament.
-- (not encoded: section 19 is parliamentary procedure for the regulation-making powers)

§§ `20 Financial provisions`

-- Section 20: sums payable by way of state pension credit, and the expenses of
-- the Act, are paid out of money provided by Parliament; any increase in sums
-- payable into the Consolidated Fund goes there. It governs the Exchequer and
-- creates no relation between a claimant and anyone. In force on the passing of
-- the Act (section 22(2)).
-- src:370 | (1) There shall be paid out of money provided by Parliament—
-- src:371 | (a) any sums payable by way of state pension credit;
-- src:372 | (b) any expenditure incurred by the Secretary of State or other government department under or by virtue of this Act; and
-- src:373 | (c) any increase attributable to this Act in the sums payable out of money so provided under any other Act.
-- src:374 | (2) There shall be paid into the Consolidated Fund any increase attributable to this Act in the sums which under any other Act are payable into that Fund.
-- (not encoded: section 20 is a financial provision between Parliament and the Exchequer)

§§ `21 Enactments repealed`

-- Section 21 repeals the enactments specified in Schedule 3, which are
-- listed (without effect on this Act's rules) in spc-sch3.l4.
-- src:376 | The enactments specified in Schedule 3 to this Act are repealed to the extent there specified.
-- (not encoded: section 21 gives effect to Schedule 3, the repeals)
